.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt VPS-DEPLOY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vps-deploy
.Nd deploy approved pub5 services to the production VPS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm all | master | brgen | amber | bsdports | mrdamascy
.Nm
.Cm recover --plan
.Nm
.Cm recover --apply
.Ar run-id
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the serialized production deploy entry point at
.Pa OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy .
Run it as
.Cm root
(or as
.Cm dev
with passwordless
.Xr doas 1 ,
which re-executes the script as root).
Git fetch and checkout always run as
.Cm dev
so the production tree and GitHub credentials stay correctly owned.
Service control and recovery receipt calls use the fixed root-owned
.Nm pub5-admin
broker directly.
When started as
.Cm dev ,
passwordless
.Xr doas 1
re-executes the script as root through
.Pa /usr/bin/env
with a prefix allowlist of
.Ev VPS_DEPLOY_*
and
.Ev PUB4_DEPLOY_*
so the pinned SHA, preflight proof, canary and logging knobs survive.
.Pp
The command validates its target, checks required local broker availability,
validates bounded timing and capacity settings, obtains the deploy lock, and
runs the configured preflight, synchronization, CI, restart, health and deploy
stamp steps.
The exact order and restore behavior are implemented in the script
and the production runbook. Every top-level run has a root-private atomic receipt
under /var/db/pub5/deploy_runs, recording the pinned SHA, previous SHA, original
running-service snapshot, ports, restore order, owner process identity and latest
stage. Child app runs update the parent receipt.
.Pp
The accepted targets are
.Cm all ,
.Cm master ,
.Cm brgen ,
.Cm amber ,
.Cm bsdports ,
and
.Cm mrdamascy .
Unknown targets are refused before deployment.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "VPS_DEPLOY_PREFLIGHT_SHA"
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_SHA
Commit to deploy.
The default is fetched from
.Cm origin/main
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_LOG
Aggregate deploy log path.
Default
.Pa /var/log/pub5/vps-deploy.log .
Rotated when larger than 10 MB.
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_LOG_DIR
Directory for aggregate and per-run logs.
Default
.Pa /var/log/pub5 .
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_RUN_LOG
Per-run log path.
Default is a timestamped file under
.Pa /var/log/pub5/runs/ .
Symlinked from
.Pa /home/dev/vps-deploy-latest.log .
once.
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_PREFLIGHT_SHA
Commit whose boot was already proved by the operator's machine.
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_CI_SHA
Commit whose
.Pa bin/ci
passed on the operator's machine.
The box installs the bundle and skips its own test suite for that commit
only, and refuses a run that would deploy any other.
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_SKIP_PREFLIGHT
Break-glass preflight bypass.
Setting this to
.Cm 1
also requires
.Ev I_UNDERSTAND_FAST_DEPLOY=1 .
.It Ev SKIP_CI
When set to
.Cm 1 ,
skips
.Pa vps_ci.sh ;
the per-application deploy script and runtime check still run.
.It Ev VPS_DEPLOY_DRIFT
Setting this to
.Cm fail
refuses deployment when machine configuration differs from the repository.
.It Ev PUB4_DEPLOY_BROWSER_CHECKS
Setting this to
.Cm 1
adds the browser checks after restart.
.El
.Ss Interrupted deployment recovery
.Pp
.Cm recover --plan
lists receipts whose service restoration is pending. It is serialized by the
deploy lock, does not fetch or check out code, and does not start, stop or
restart services. A receipt is reported as live when its owner PID and process
fingerprint still match, ambiguous when that PID cannot be identified, and
available only when the recorded process is gone or the PID has been reused.
.Pp
.Cm recover --apply
.Ar run-id
requires the exact ID shown by the plan. It refuses a live or ambiguous owner,
restores only services captured as running before that deploy, in the recorded
order, and verifies brokered service state plus each recorded app's loopback
.Pa /up
endpoint. Success marks the receipt recovered. A failed verification leaves it
pending for diagnosis and a later explicit retry.
.Pp
Recovery restores service availability only. It does not roll back the Git
checkout, database migrations or application data. It is never run automatically
at boot. The installed broker must support the deploy-run verbs; install and
verify the reviewed mirror before the first use of this receipt-enabled deployer.
.Sh SECURITY
Do not run as root.
Do not bypass preflight during ordinary deployments.
A
successful synchronization or TLS response alone does not establish that every
application is healthy.
Inspect the actual health and deploy receipt.
.Pp
Before live work, read
.Pa OPENBSD/RUNBOOK.md
and the owning tree README.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy --help
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy master
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy all
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy recover --plan
zsh OPENBSD/bin/vps-deploy recover --apply 20261117T010000Z-all-12345
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr operator 1 ,
.Xr pub5-admin 8 ,
.Xr rcctl 8 ,
.Xr relayd 8
